description: Feature-based architecture and shared-layer boundaries
alwaysApply: true
---

# Project Architecture

- Follow Feature-Based Architecture.
- Every feature contains only what it needs (no empty folders):
  - api/ · components/ · hooks/ · screens/ · services/ · types/ · utils/ · assets/ · db/

- **Feature assets:** if an image is used only by one feature, keep it under `src/features/<name>/assets/` and require it relatively from that feature. Shared brand assets (logo, spinner, onboarding art, etc.) stay in `src/assets/` and are consumed via `IMAGES` from `@shared/constants`.
- Shared code lives under `src/shared/` (organized by use):
  - `api/` — Axios client + errors`business/` · `services/` (legacy HTTP helpers)
  - `components/` — shared UI for features.
  - `ui/` - shared UI elements (input, button etc.).
- Core shell lives under `src/core/`:
  - `context/` — app-owned providers/hooks
  - `providers/` — `AppProviders` composition (SafeArea, Keyboard)
  - `db/` — shared SQLite client, migration provider, schema aggregation
  - `env/` — typed public env (`@core/env`); read `EXPO_PUBLIC_*` from `.env` only through this module
  - `storage/secure-store/` — SecureStore infrastructure + public token-storage
  - `App.js` is entry + SDK bootstrap only;
- **Theme:** colors, typography, spacing, radius, touch, layout only in [`src/theme/tokens.js`](src/theme/tokens.js) (`@app/theme/tokens`). Must stay in sync with `.cursor/rules/design.mdc`. Do not invent new tokens. Use `textStyle(variant)` for RN text styles (maps Inter weights to loaded font faces). Keep theme outside `src/app` so Expo Router does not register it as a route.
- Features import from `@shared/*`, their own `@features/<name>/*`, `@app/theme/*`, `@/core/context/*`, `@core/env`, `@core/db` (client only when inside that feature’s repository), and the public core storage surface `@/core/storage/secure-store` — never from root `@utils`, `@components`.
- Never import from another feature except through that feature’s public `index` exports.

# Local database

- `@core/db` owns the shared Expo SQLite + Drizzle **client**, `DatabaseProvider` (migrations), and schema **aggregation** only.
- Feature-owned local data lives under `features/<name>/db/` (`schema`, `repository`) with `services/` that call the repository.
- Call flow for local persistence: **service → repository → db**.
- Screens, components, and hooks outside the owning feature must not query `db` directly — use that feature’s public API (e.g. `@features/user`).
- The owning feature’s repository is the only layer that talks to the shared `db` client.
- `users` table (owned by `@features/user`) caches the logged-in user and conversation participant profiles.

# Secure storage

- `expo-secure-store` and `src/core/storage/secure-store/secureStore.ts` are **private**. Do not import them from features, shared, or anywhere else.
- Public API is **only** `@/core/storage/secure-store` (`token-storage`: `saveTokens`, `getAccessToken`, `getRefreshToken`, `deleteTokens`).
- Axios (`@/shared/api`) attaches the access token via `getAccessToken` on authenticated requests.
- Auth flows persist/clear tokens with `saveTokens` / `deleteTokens` — never by calling SecureStore directly.

# Navigation Stack

- `Auth Stack` (`(auth)`): Welcome, Login, Signup — when user is not logged in.
- `Home Stack` (`(home)`): **Bottom Tabs** for Conversations (tab label "Chats"), Search and About after logged in.
- Root `index` redirects by auth status; splash waits for fonts + auth bootstrap.
